A||||9||FLASHY||EuroWorks Lamborghini kits question||||5||
Z||000000||FLASHY||10-15-2001||01:19 AM||||Now that I hear Lamborghini is attemptimg to stop production of Lambo kits, I'm starting to want some serious answers for possible near-future purchasing before it's too late.<P>Does anybody know the quality and reliability of EuroWorks' kits? I've always liked their Mirage K kit (Non-stretched style) and wondered if they are as good as they say. Has anyone here actually built or is building one of their kits? <P>I'm just wondering if they make the best kits (Non-stretched) or is there another company that's better in your opinion? Any answers would be great. Thanks!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Oh, and I have done a search and didn't find much on them other than "they are good". I'd like more info if possible.<P>Here's a link. <A HREF="http://www.euroworksltd.com/MirageK/MirageKSpec.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euroworksltd.com/MirageK/MirageKSpec.htm</A> <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spinsig3.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||FLASHY||10-15-2001||09:34 AM||||*BUMP* Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||10-15-2001||11:00 AM||||I've heard nothing but good things about the Euro-Works company. They stand by their product and offer excellent support. <P>I got kicked out of their display booth two times in Carlisle! That yellow V8 kit was awesome! I couldn't stop drooling all over it! I don't remember if it was a stretch or not. <P>The man I talked to was very nice, took time to talk with me and answer questions. They're who I'd buy through!||||reg||14
Z||000003||FLASHY||10-15-2001||02:05 PM||||Wow, that's good to know. Thanks torbo86se! I sent an email to them asking a few questions. We'll see what they say.<P>Anyone else?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero_24||10-15-2001||05:45 PM||||I have spoken to the owner several times, and he has always answered my questions.  He even called me from his cell phone once (long distance) to tell me more about the kits.  It is just too bad I could not come up with the money to buy the kit.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||14
Z||000005||rogergarrison||10-15-2001||05:57 PM||||there stuffs great and affordable. I think they may be the only ones making a non stretch body. Dont look as accurate but who cares. Also make note, they JUST released a NON stretch Diablo kit also. There only about 60 miles away from me, and Ive checked them out.<P>There is a complete body kit on Ebay right now and a seperate donor 85 4cyl for less than $3000 rite now in Chicago area. I dont have the link handy, but go to ebaymotors and seach 'other makes/kitcars'<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 10-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||RossT||10-15-2001||08:58 PM||||Flashy, Check out the lambo pics I posted recently.  If you are serious, let me know and I will put you in touch with the owner.  His kit is a Euroworks kit, and he has some good things to say, but also alot of bad things to say. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||10-15-2001||10:15 PM||||Be forewarned- these ARE NOT bolt on kits, you have to do a lot of frame cutting and a whole bunch of welding and bracket making||||reg||1
Z||000008||RossT||10-16-2001||12:05 AM||||Yes, Phil said it!!  Jason has been working on his for almost 5 years and has about 20K invested.. Lots of fabrication too..<P>Need to ask Rockcrawl how long his took..||||reg||1
Z||000009||FLASHY||10-16-2001||12:50 AM||||Did Rockcrawl use a EuroWorks kit too? And was it a stretched or non-stretched? And I can tell by RossT's pics that the Lambo kit pictured is a stretched one which is supposed to be much more work. Even if it took me 5 years to build one I'd say it's still worth it though.<P>Oh, and I know there is atleast one other company who makes a non-stretched countach kit. They're called the Lamboshop. I recently posted a topic on one of their kits for sale on ebay.<P>Here's their website. <A HREF="http://www.lamboshop.com/frames2.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lamboshop.com/frames2.htm</A> <P>I actually like the look of their kits better than EuroWorks but am not sure of their quality, reliability, and if the price is right.||||reg||1
